Summary: Rosetta 2: report success when a thread sets its own debug registers
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 22131
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
  Note: identical to CrossOver 25.1.1's. Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it:
    ntdll.so: "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta,
    faking success" (its wineserver also has CW HACK 21217's "%04x:
    thread_get_state failed on Apple Silicon - faking zero debug
    registers", which WineHQ's is_rosetta() in server/mach.c makes
    unneeded, 10.0 included; CrossOver 26.3.0 no longer carries 21217)
  Changes: verbatim
Upstream: partly (wineserver already returns zeroed debug registers under
 Rosetta and refuses to set them, is_rosetta() in server/mach.c, 10.0
 included; reporting success is not upstream)
Why: Rosetta 2 can't set x86 debug registers, so wineserver refuses when
 a thread sets its own (server/mach.c, is_rosetta()), and
 NtSetContextThread fails, dropping the other registers in the same call
 as well. Report success instead, from NtSetContextThread and the wow64
 set-context path: Wine keeps the values, so the thread reads back what
 it set, but no hardware breakpoint fires. Anti-debug and DRM code that
 sets debug registers on itself (Armadillo) then carries on.
Programs: Big Fish games (Armadillo DRM): setting debug registers fails
 under Rosetta (Armadillo's parent relies on the faked success)
Messages: "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta, faking
 success" (warn:seh; shown only with WINEDEBUG=warn+seh)
Uncertain: a program that sets a hardware breakpoint and waits for it
 now gets success and no breakpoint, instead of an error
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: now this copy (the 10.0 copy's dead wineserver
 half dropped). debug-registers passed on 10.0 build0
 with the old copy (2026-11-25, i686 and x86_64).
 11.22: 2026-11-25: debug-registers passes on the 11.22 quick build (i686
 and x86_64, "faking success" logged twice per run); not run without it.
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T013940 and T024442 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed
 11.21: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T005336 and T023339 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed
 11.22: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T002454 and T025644 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 7bff70b..adc9260 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -1003,7 +1003,11 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetContextThread( HANDLE handle, const CONTEXT *context )
         ret = set_thread_context( handle, context, &self, IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_AMD64 );
 #ifdef __APPLE__
         if ((flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) && (ret == STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL))
-            WARN_(seh)( "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta\n" );
+        {
+            /* CW HACK 22131 */
+            WARN_(seh)( "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta, faking success\n" );
+            ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+        }
 #endif
         if (ret || !self) return ret;
         if (flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
@@ -1234,6 +1238,14 @@ NTSTATUS set_thread_wow64_context( HANDLE handle, const void *ctx, ULONG size )
     if (!self)
     {
         NTSTATUS ret = set_thread_context( handle, context, &self, IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386 );
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        if ((flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) && (ret == STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL))
+        {
+            /* CW HACK 22131 */
+            WARN_(seh)( "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta, faking success\n" );
+            ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+        }
+#endif
         if (ret || !self) return ret;
         if (flags & CONTEXT_I386_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
         {
